    "updated_at": "2021-05-10T05:05:56Z",
    "body": "> `getImageDataInto(x, y, destination)`\r\n> \r\n> It seems that should fail though if destination points to a detached buffer so you cannot transfer to workers, but rather have to copy, right?\r\n\r\nThat seems totally fine, because the memory can first be transferred back from a worker, then this method can be called, then the buffer can be transferred back to the worker. The whole time only (effectively) pointers would sent back and forth. EDIT: Oh, that's what @Kaiido said.\r\n\r\nTransferred `Transferable` objects should never be re-usable on the original thread where they were before being transferred.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
